<title>DUBAI: Oman lifts October crude price to $22.50.</title>
<headline>Oman lifts October crude price to $22.50.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1996-11-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oman has increased the price of its crude lifted in October by $1.30 to $22.50, an official at the Omani Ministry of Petroleum and Minerals said.</p>
<p>The October price is the highest level so far this year for Oman crude.</p>
<p>The higher official selling prices reflect strong crude markets and premiums for Oman grades last month.</p>
<p>Oman, a major non-OPEC producer, retroactively sets its crude price every month.</p>
<p>-- Steven Swindells, Dubai Newsroom, +971 4 6071255.</p>
</text>
